hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27689","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Akhbarana Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Maqburi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bujayd, from his grandmother Umm Bujayd, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, the poor man stands at my door until I am shy, and I find nothing in my house to lift into his hand. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Lift into his hand even a burnt hoof."
"27690","Haddathana Hajjaj and Abu Kamil, they both said: Haddathana Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, he said: Sa'id, meaning al-Maqburi, narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bujayd, brother of Banu Harithah, that his grandmother, wife of Bujayd, narrated to him, and she claimed to be among those who pledged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned its meaning."
"27691","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim: Haddathana al-Layth: Sa'id, meaning al-Maqburi, narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bujayd, brother of Banu Harithah, that his grandmother, who is Umm Bujayd, narrated to him, and she was among those who pledged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: By Allah, the poor man stands at my door and I find nothing to give him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: If you find nothing to give him except a burnt hoof, push it into his hand."
"27692","Haddathana Affan, he said: Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bujayd, from his grandmother Umm Bujayd, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to us in Banu Amr ibn Awf, and I would make for him a sawiq drink in a bowl of mine, and when he came I would give him to drink. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the beggar comes to me and I scorn some of what I have for him. So he said: Put in the hand of the poor even a burnt hoof."
"27693","Haddathana Waki', he said: Haddathana Sufyan, from Mansur ibn Hayyan al-Asadi, from Ibn Bijad, from his grandmother, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Return the beggar even with a burnt or scorched sheep hoof."
